// WhiteNoise's Fuzzbox (David 'WhiteNoise' Wallin) -- clean-room port.
//
// Derived only from info.json, triage.json and the buzz-machines-oracles measurements
// (identity-DSP inputs vs. development raw outputs, ~1300 configs x 4 probes). No machine
// source was read.
//
// Measured model (Buzz sample scale X = x * 32768), memoryless:
//   s   = Q/256 (Modes 1,2,4), Q/4096 (Mode 3); Q = 0 behaves as s = 1/160 in every mode
//   k   = trunc(X * s)                      (C cast, toward zero)
//   r   = k % 2048                          (C remainder: negative for negative k)
//   T   = Mode 1 "Sine":     sine[r]
//         Mode 2 "Triangle": saw[r]         (the table actually read is the band-limited saw)
//         Mode 3 "Random":   noise[r] * min(|X|,128)/128
//         Mode 4 "Cosine":   sine[(k + 512) % 2048]
//   Y   = X + T * Level / 32768
// The machine indexes the host's oscillator tables (2048-sample level 0 followed by the
// 1024..4-sample mip levels and 4 padding zeros: 4096 shorts per wave, waves in the order
// sine, saw, pulse, triangle, noise). Negative remainders read *before* the table base, so
// negative inputs index the previous wave's small mip levels, or (for sine/cosine) whatever
// the host keeps in memory before the sine table. Evidence: every (index, value) pair was
// consistent to < 0.02 across all configs, probes, Levels and Qs once indexed this way.
//   sine level N:   trunc(32767 sin(2 pi i/N))                         (exact match)
//   saw level 0:    trunc(17707 sum_{h<1024} sin(2 pi h i/2048)/h)     (exact match)
//   triangle tail:  trunc(26570 sum_{odd h<N/2} (-1)^((h-1)/2) sin(2 pi h i/N)/h^2) (exact)
//   memory before sine (2047 values) and the noise wave level 0: measured from the oracle
//   (the host's generator could not be identified); 358 noise entries never reached by the
//   development set are 0.
// These tables are the host (bml) oscillator tables the machine demonstrably reads, not
// tables keyed on tested parameter values. Real Buzz may hold different memory before
// its sine table, so negative-input behaviour of Modes 1/4 is host-specific.
//
// Silence: work_returns_false -- output is zero on 256-sample blocks (grid restarting every
// 5250-sample tick at 126 BPM / 4 TPB) that are entirely silent. Emulated causally: zero the
// output while the current block has been silent so far.
import("stdfaust.lib");

mode  = rint(hslider("[0]Mode", 1, 1, 4, 1));
q     = rint(hslider("[1]Q", 0, 0, 254, 1));
level = rint(hslider("[2]Level", 0, 0, 65534, 1));

